---
import './design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from './SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from './SketchArrow.astro';
---
<figure id="data-type-comparison" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface type-comparison" aria-labelledby="type-comparison-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Data types and ordering</span>
  <h3 id="type-comparison-title">The same digits, a different order</h3>
  <div class="orderings">
    <section aria-labelledby="integer-order-title">
      <h4 id="integer-order-title">Numbers · <code>integer</code></h4>
      <p class="rule">Compare numeric value</p>
      <div class="ordered-sheet">
        <div class="direction"><span>Ascending</span><SketchArrow direction="down" /></div>
        <SketchSheet>
          <ol class="records numeric-records" aria-label="Integers in ascending order">
            <li><code>2</code><span>Smallest value</span></li>
            <li><code>10</code></li>
            <li><code>100</code><span>Largest value</span></li>
          </ol>
        </SketchSheet>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="text-order-title">
      <h4 id="text-order-title">Strings · <code>text</code></h4>
      <p class="rule">Compare characters from left to right<br /><small>PostgreSQL <code>COLLATE "C"</code></small></p>
      <div class="ordered-sheet">
        <div class="direction"><span>Ascending</span><SketchArrow direction="down" /></div>
        <SketchSheet>
          <ol class="records text-records" aria-label="Strings in ascending order with PostgreSQL C collation">
            <li><code>'<span class="prefix">10</span>'</code><span>Ends after <code>10</code></span></li>
            <li><code>'<span class="prefix">10</span>0'</code><span>Same prefix, then <code>0</code></span></li>
            <li><code>'<span class="later">2</span>'</code><span><code>2</code> comes after <code>1</code></span></li>
          </ol>
        </SketchSheet>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Representation changes comparison. Integers sort by magnitude. These strings sort character by character under PostgreSQL’s <code>"C"</code> collation: <code>'10'</code> ends before <code>'100'</code>, and both begin with <code>1</code>, before <code>2</code>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .orderings { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1.8rem; margin-top:1.3rem; }
  .orderings section { min-width:0; margin:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }
  .orderings h4 { margin-bottom:.25rem; }
  .design-figure .rule { margin:0 0 .85rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.8rem; flex:1; }
  .rule small { font-size:.72rem; }
  .ordered-sheet { display:grid; grid-template-columns:2.8rem minmax(0,1fr); align-items:stretch; gap:.25rem; }
  .direction { display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:1rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .direction > span { writing-mode:vertical-rl; font-size:.73rem; }
  .direction :global(svg) { width:2.6rem; }
  .records { margin:0; padding:0; list-style:none; }
  .records li { min-height:4.4rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; gap:.25rem; padding:.5rem .4rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
  .records li:last-child { border-bottom:0; }
  .records li > code { width:max-content; font:500 1.4rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); white-space:nowrap; }
  .records li > span { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.72rem; line-height:1.4; }
  .numeric-records li > code { color:var(--teal); }
  .prefix { background:var(--paper-match); border-bottom:1px solid var(--teal); }
  .later { background:var(--paper-highlight); border-bottom:1px solid var(--gold); }
  @media(max-width:600px) {
    .orderings { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:1.7rem; max-width:23rem; margin-inline:auto; }
    .records li { flex-direction:row; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:.8rem; min-height:3.6rem; }
    .records li > span { max-width:9rem; }
  }
</style>
